-3.1 For any test function with $\|\phi\|_\infty+\operatorname{Lip}(\phi)\le1$, the initial cohort pushforward differs from the first integral for $\widehat n$ in step 1.1 by at most $C_T(\epsilon_0+\Delta t)$, using step 2.1 and the bounded-Lipschitz norm of $x\mapsto\phi(x+t)S(x,t)$. The newborn cohort sum differs from the second integral by its left-Riemann error $C_T\Delta t$ plus $\Delta t\sum_{j<k}e_j\le C_T(\epsilon_0+\Delta t)$ by step 2.2. Thus $\|\nu_h^k-\widehat n(t_k,a)da\|_{BL^*}\le C_T(\epsilon_0+\Delta t)$. The initial data difference is $\|n_0-\widehat n_0\|_1=\tau_A$, so [F5] gives $\|n(t_k)-\widehat n(t_k)\|_1\le e^{\beta_\infty T}\tau_A$. The inequality $\|f(a)da\|_{BL^*}\le\|f\|_1$ and the triangle inequality prove the stated bound. [F1, F2, F5, step 1.1, step 2.1, step 2.2, algebra] ∎
